  "articleBody": "Laundry rooms can be surprisingly hazardous if we're not careful. It's easy to overlook simple things that can lead to big problems. Let's talk about some common mistakes and how to avoid them. First, relying on plastic flex hoses for dryer venting is a no-go; they're fire hazards. Always opt for fire-resistant venting instead. Second, ignoring lint buildup, whether it's in the screen or deep in the ducts, is a major fire risk. Clean that screen after every load, and get your ducts professionally cleaned periodically. Third, storing harsh chemicals like detergents and bleach within easy reach of kids or pets is a huge mistake. Invest in locked cabinets or high shelving. Fourth, using extension cords for your washer or dryer is dangerous; these appliances need proper, fixed outlets. Finally, don't ignore small leaks! Even tiny drips can lead to electrical hazards or significant water damage over time. Addressing these issues promptly can prevent much bigger headaches. If you're unsure about any of these safety aspects, especially when water, electricity, and ventilation issues overlap, it's wise to bring in a pro like HH Remodeling LLC.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}